** Diameter of a Tree (2 DFS)

The longest path between any two nodes in the tree, whether it passes through the Root or not.
// Idea: 1. DFS from any node -> farNode.  2. DFS from farNode -> Maximum distance = Diameter.
// Property:The farthest node from any node is always one endpoint of the diameter.
// Time: O(N) &&  Space: O(N)

vector<vector<int>> adj;
int mx, dist, farNode;
void dfs(int node, int par){
    for(auto child : adj[node]){
        if(child == par) continue;
        dist++;
        if(dist > mx){
            mx = dist;
            farNode = child;
        }
        dfs(child, node);
        dist--;      // Backtracking
    }
}
// 1st DFS
dist = 0; mx = 0; dfs(1, 0);
// 2nd DFS
dist = 0;  mx = 0; dfs(farNode, 0);
cout << mx;

